# Who must approve what (SEC-K, #847; Jonathan's decisions of 15/11 and 18/11): the files that a
# workflow holding a secret, a write permission or an OIDC token runs, the CD of Imladris, and the
# bench's Terraform — nothing else, so that every other pull request merges as before, without
# waiting for anyone.
#
# Not here, by decision (18/11): the Makefile. Its recipes run with the maintainer's own rights —
# `make imladris-cd-install` among them, which copies the CD's files and discord.env to Imladris and
# runs install.sh there as root. So the CD of Imladris is owned here for its files, not for the
# recipe that installs them: a follow-up lot moves that recipe into a script under
# infra/glorfindel-host/cd/, owned with the rest. docs/design/modele-de-menace.md, §7.
#
# It holds once the maintainer has turned on « Require review from Code Owners » in main's rule —
# after this file is merged, never before (with the former `*` line, every pull request would have
# waited for him). Then a pull request that touches one of these paths waits for his approval: the
# sessions' App, which has no Workflows right, can no longer change unseen what runs with the
# secrets by changing a script outside .github/workflows/. Until then, it is indicative only.
#
# tests/unit/test_codeowners.py keeps this list against the workflows: it reads each job of
# .github/workflows/ that holds a secret, a write permission or `id-token: write`, takes the files of
# the repository it runs (named in a `run:`, a local action, the code of a sparse checkout, a
# requirements file it installs, what a script imports next to it or a shell script calls next to
# it), adds what Imladris's CD installs (AGENT_FILES), and fails when one of them has no line here —
# or when a line owns none of them, but the four directories owned whole (DECIDED in the test). The form it reads: one
# owner, the maintainer; an anchored path, a file or a directory (a trailing /), no pattern.
# docs/design/modele-de-menace.md, §6 and §7.

# The CI itself, this file included.
/.github/                               @grootcyber

# publish.yml: the OIDC token that signs the images, packages: write, attestations: write.
/scripts/published_image.py             @grootcyber
/scripts/image_check.py                 @grootcyber
/scripts/retry.sh                       @grootcyber

# notify.yml, roadmap.yml: the Discord secrets of the workshop (its sparse checkout, all of it).
/scripts/notify_discord.py              @grootcyber
/scripts/roadmap_discord.py             @grootcyber
/glorfindel/chat_text.py                @grootcyber
/.claude/skills/elrond/palantir.py      @grootcyber

# pip-audit.yml: issues: write — the script, and the lock of the pip-audit it installs.
/scripts/pip_audit_issues.py            @grootcyber
/requirements/audit.txt                 @grootcyber

# canary-azurerm.yml: the canary's OIDC token (Network Contributor on its group).
/infra/canary/                          @grootcyber

# The CD of Imladris, and what it installs next to it (AGENT_FILES).
/infra/glorfindel-host/cd/              @grootcyber
/infra/glorfindel-host/deploy.sh        @grootcyber

# The bench's Terraform (decision of 18/11): its local-exec provisioners run with the rights of
# whoever applies, at `terraform apply`, and never show in the plan.
/infra/terraform/                       @grootcyber
